    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1045">

                <pb facs="0652" n="1702" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p2/pg1702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.919/7–2953: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Allen</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1045-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-07-29T19:00:00+05:30">July 29, 1953—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>215. Re Embtels 190, July 25<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1045-f2"/> and 192, July 26. Embassy has received note dated July
                    29 from MEA in reply Embassy’s note July 25,
                    stating small shipment of thorium nitrate made to China with permission GOI; that consignment of thorium nitrate already
                    paid for and ownership passed other hands; and GOI thus not in position to “offload this consignment or to deal
                    with it in any other way at this stage”.</p>
                <p>In conversations today between Pillai and
                    myself and between Mani and Drumright,
                    both MEA officials stressed small quantity
                    thorium nitrate involved, desire of GOI to sell
                    thorium nitrate to US Government, and hinted GOI
                    prepared carry out effective administrative controls strategic material but not
                    in position give open commitment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Allen</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1045-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1045-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated to London as telegram 25, to Colombo as telegram 10,
                    to Singapore as telegram 7, and to Hong Kong as telegram 6.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1045-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1045-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 1 to telegram 192, <ref target="#pg1697">p. 1697</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
